What was taken, and from where:

- `native/app/src/pane_screen.rs` (the `PaneScreen` component) follows the drawing design of nsh's
  `Terminal` component (`crates/nsh-base/src/term/mod.rs` on nsh `main`, added in commit c8e044b;
  not part of the nsh 0.4.0 release this app is built on): a virtualized list of one-row views,
  the cells' backgrounds drawn as boxes behind the text because a text span's background covers
  only the glyphs' ink, runs drawn as nested text spans in one selectable text per row, and the
  cell width measured from the font as a tenth of the width of ten zeros. The emulator, the
  pseudo-terminal sink and the input handling of `Terminal` were not used.
- `native/core/src/screen/contrast.rs` (`indexed_cube_rgb`) computes the xterm 6x6x6 colour cube
  and 24 greys with the same level formula as `Terminal`'s `indexed()` function (cube levels
  `0` and `55 + 40n`, greys `8 + 10n`); the first 16 colours come from this app's theme instead of
  `Terminal`'s fixed palette.

